From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 20:02:34 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 49/72] deepseek: split long prefill index selections by rows
 over TP2 (TF_DSV41_IDX_SPLIT)

Each rank selects only its rows of a prefill segment's index layers and the
two ranks all-gather the int32 selection rows before the counts read them:
ids move, no arithmetic. Rows keep the replicated loop's per-row launches
(its own block boundary when it has one, else an even 64-row cut). The
candidate source keeps its candidates on their rank; its reindex layers
take the same cut.

TF_DSV41_IDX_SPLIT: unset / 0 / off = the replicated programs (default),
auto = rows x visible keys >= 4,096 x 65,536, 1 = every TP2 segment of 256
rows or more. Both ranks exchange the mode at boot and refuse to start when
they differ. The plan sizes the gather for ragged segments, and aot-needs
lists the other rank's split programs and the replicated ones.

Mechanism after MiaAI-Lab DeepSeek-v4.1-Flash-1017-2x-DGX-Sparks patch
0001-c7-indexer-split (Apache-2.0, idea credited there to drowzeys) and
vLLM #54951 / #61647; re-implemented for this emitter, no code copied.
